{
    "background_story": "Kalani was a brilliant and daring engineer who had always been fascinated by the art of suspension. Growing up in a family of circus performers, she was accustomed to the thrill of being airborne. Kalani's passion led her to design innovative suspension systems for high-rise buildings and bridges. Her creations were not only structurally sound but also breathtakingly beautiful. One of her most notable projects was the 'SkyDance' bridge, a suspended pedestrian walkway that seemed to defy gravity. As people walked across, they felt as though they were floating above the city. Kalani's work was a masterclass in combining art and science, leaving onlookers in a state of suspensory wonder. Her legacy continued to inspire generations of engineers and architects to push the boundaries of what was thought possible.",
